fying Open and Closed Sets in the Plane in Set Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2d38a336-527b-57b5-984e-edfc2714a948" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435723} {:answer/id #uuid "596ac92d-b0b2-508d-8d21-57fdf30094ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435725} {:answer/id #uuid "7a873c8b-abd6-5688-a8dc-2234e4f321c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435729} {:answer/id #uuid "b92f330b-d989-5fa6-a357-1f8fb2911ce0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435733} {:answer/id #uuid "d390df63-e312-58d7-be1f-9359c50c2171" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435734}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7a873c8b-abd6-5688-a8dc-2234e4f321c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435729} :answer-field/id #uuid "31c038cd-735d-510d-a7a3-1258bc6d67c1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435737}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0c87d140-5d2b-5665-af2c-c72dc631274f" :question/math-academy-id "q-161645" :question/problem "Which of the following sets are open?\n\nI. $\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}:\\text{ }2\\le x\\le 3,\\,1\\le y\\le x\\}$\n\nII. $\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}:\\text{ }1\\le {x}^{2}\\le 4,\\,1\\le y\\le 2\\}$\n\nIII. $\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}:\\text{ }5{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<2\\}$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that:\n\n- A set is *open* if it does not contain any of its boundary points. In other words, an open set consists only of the interior points of the set.\n\n- A set is *closed* if it contains **all** of its boundary points. In other words, a closed set consists of all the interior and all the boundary points of the set.\n\nLet's examine our sets in turn.\n\n- The first set is *closed* since it contains all of its boundary points (all the corresponding inequalities are not strict).\n\n- The second set is *closed* since it contains all of its boundary points (all the corresponding inequalities are not strict).\n\n- The third set is *open* since it doesn't contain any of its boundary points (all the corresponding inequalities are strict).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278582 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192767 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7adf2c3e-4a73-5098-ab60-790d637728cf" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Open and Closed Sets in the Plane in Set Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f43270e-5fd5-5fe3-b96d-2845968d906e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275762} {:answer/id #uuid "91704fdf-0254-5001-b4f6-f9904429324d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276793} {:answer/id #uuid "ade20714-3320-54e9-8da1-4e2411c22400" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277039} {:answer/id #uuid "edcf9c63-cf2d-53a3-bf2a-463a56016f93" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277565} {:answer/id #uuid "ede4ae0d-2c59-565f-940e-2e848fb5dec5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id 